---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Dance with B collects and uses your registration and contact information."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-extrabold text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">What we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">
          When you register for a class, check in, or contact us through this site, we collect the information you
          submit: your name, phone number and/or email, the class or event you selected, and any notes or messages
          you include.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">How we use it</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">
          We use your contact information only to reach you about your registration — confirmations, class or
          schedule changes, cancellations, or a question you asked us directly.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          After you come to a class or event, we may also add you to a WhatsApp group or community, so we can share
          important updates such as the lesson recaps included with your purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">What we don't do</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">
          We never sell, rent, or share your contact information with any third party or external entity. It stays
          with us and is used solely for the purpose above.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Push notifications</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">
          Notifications are off unless you turn them on from the bell at the top of the site. When you do, your browser
          gives us an address its notification service uses to reach your phone. We keep only that address and whether
          it's an iPhone or Android phone (to count them), never your name or contact details, and use it only to tell
          you about new classes, events and workshops. Turn notifications off with the same switch (or in your phone's settings) and the
          address is deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">We use a small amount of local browser storage to remember basic preferences, like your cookie choice or that you've already seen a tip on the homepage.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink">Questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-1">
          If you have any questions about this policy or your information, reach out through our{' '}
          <a href="/contact" class="text-accent underline hover:no-underline">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
